---
import { LinkButton } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

const roots = [
  {
    name: 'htmx',
    url: 'https://htmx.org',
    showed:
      'that the browser already is a hypermedia client, and only needed a few more verbs. Any element can make a request, the server answers with HTML, and the page swaps it in. Server-sent events carry updates.',
    keeps: ['the server sends HTML', 'boosted links and forms', 'event streams for updates'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Alpine.js',
    url: 'https://alpinejs.dev',
    showed:
      'that state and behaviour belong next to the markup they drive. x-data, x-model and x-show made reactive attributes feel like HTML, with expressions that are simply JavaScript.',
    keeps: ['state declared in attributes', 'expressions as plain JavaScript', 'the attribute style itself'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Datastar',
    url: 'https://data-star.dev',
    showed:
      'that the two ideas are one. Signals in the browser and patches from the server share a single attribute vocabulary, and the server can drive the page as easily as the page drives itself.',
    keeps: ['the attribute vocabulary', 'signals and server patches together', 'markup written for it runs unchanged'],
  },
];
---
<section class="home-s not-content">
  <h2>Three libraries made this one possible.</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    sigmx is not a new idea. It is a small, independent implementation of ideas three libraries proved first, and it
    would not exist without them. If you already use one, you will feel at home.
  </p>
  <div class="roots">
    {roots.map((r) => (
      <article>
        <h3><a href={r.url} rel="noopener">{r.name}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3>
        <p><em>Showed</em> {r.showed}</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="k">what sigmx keeps</li>
          {r.keeps.map((k) => <li>{k}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="lede after">
    What is different is the implementation: no shared code, a smaller and simpler codebase, plugins you register
    rather than side effects that register themselves, and a build that does the heavy lifting. <a href="/start/introduction/">The introduction</a> tells the full story.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="home-s not-content start">
  <h2>A script tag, or an npm install.</h2>
  <div class="row">
    <code class="install"><span>$</span> npm install sigmx</code>
    <div class="actions">
      <LinkButton href="/start/installation/" icon="right-arrow">Get started</LinkButton>
      <LinkButton href="/examples/" variant="minimal">See the examples</LinkButton>
      <LinkButton href="https://github.com/wrux/sigmx" variant="minimal" icon="github" iconPlacement="start">GitHub</LinkButton>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .roots {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 54rem) {
    .roots {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }
  article {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  h3 a {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  h3 a span {
    margin-left: 0.3rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  h3 a:hover span {
    color: var(--sl-color-accent);
  }
  article p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  article em {
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  article ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  article li::before {
    content: '·';
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-accent);
  }
  article li.k {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }
  article li.k::before {
    content: none;
  }
  .after {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .start .row {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
  }
  .install {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .install span {
    color: var(--sl-color-accent);
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
